      "expected": "The specification states the LiDAR is documentation only and not wired: 'the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no, in_bom: yes, and all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design.'",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Water Height Sensor: PR1 LIDAR ... H4 PB_1.25mm ... I2C_SDA / I2C_SCL"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no, in_bom: yes, and all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design."}
      ],
      "impact": "If a TF-Luna module is fitted it would appear as an extra device on the main I2C bus (shared with the EZO-RTD, BME280 and BH1750), contrary to the intended design in which the LiDAR is unconnected and water level is read by the HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing is largely consistent with the specification, but one clear component-value error stands out: C59, the 24 V bulk capacitor for the Nutrient-A TMC2209 driver, is 220n whereas the identical capacitors in the other two driver blocks are 220µ. A second, lower-confidence discrepancy is that the TF-Luna LiDAR (PR1) appears wired to the I2C bus even though the specification states it is not connected to any net."
}

